## Git Branching Strategy (College Decision 2026-09-01)
- `master` is the clean, production-ready canonical branch. Direct unverified commits by agents to `master` are strictly forbidden.
- Feature and experiment work must occur on `feat/*` or `exp/*` branches.
- Merging to `master` requires passing a clean Gatekeeper checklist: `gitDirty=false`, matching build fingerprint, and zero stability regressions against `stable-pd`.
- `git checkout` is strictly forbidden while the Unity Editor is running. Parallel subagents must use isolated `git worktree` and distinct build/trial output folders (`-BuildFolder`, `-TrialFolder`).

Do not delete or rename `Trials/Baselines/*`, `Trials/Runs/*`,
`.cursor/tasks/archive/`. Do not "clean" Runs. Do not backfill fingerprint
in `legacy-no-provenance/`. A new baseline only from a card.

If two files disagree, fix the pointer; do not drop the old table.
`current-front.mdc` is append-only.

